<!--
Shared LLM instructions. Keep tool-neutral — portable behavior rules only.
-->

# Instructions

## Asking the user

- When you present choices (AskUserQuestion tool), I must always be able to
  answer in free text instead of picking a predefined option. The harness adds
  a "Type something" free-text entry and a "Chat about this" entry to every
  question automatically — do not add your own free-form option, it is already
  there.
- NEVER use the `preview` field on options (the bordered side-by-side form) —
  it is banned.
- When you ask more than one question at once, add a final extra question
  titled "Extra" (or similar), with exactly two options and no descriptions:
  "Nothing to add" and "—" (a filler, since the tool requires at least two
  options). I write anything extra via the automatic "Type something".

## Reviewing diffs

- When working from the CLI and the `revdiff` skill is available, show me diffs
  and proposed edits in revdiff (TUI overlay) by default — do NOT print the diff
  as text in chat. This applies everywhere, not just one project.
- A proposed edit goes to revdiff FIRST — never print a proposed diff as text,
  even before I approve it. Text in chat is only for asking confirmation.
- Launch revdiff yourself (the launcher opens an overlay in my terminal); I
  annotate whole-file or per-line, and the annotations come back to you as
  `file:line (type)` text.
- To show proposed edits WITHOUT touching real files: one file — `--compare-old=<real,
  resolve symlinks first, else the diff shows every line as added>`
  `--compare-new=<temp copy>`; several files — make them in a temp git worktree and launch
  revdiff from there (with `--untracked`, else new files are invisible). Apply only after
  I approve; quitting revdiff with no annotations IS approval, unless the launcher timed
  out into the background — then ask first. Don't pipe a patch into the launcher —
  `--stdin` never reaches it.
- Pass chat context (what to look at, your questions) via `--description` so I
  can read it inside the overlay.
- Once a change was shown in revdiff, do NOT reprint the diff as text — just ask
  for confirmation if you need it.

## Local instructions

For additional local instructions, see following files
- @~/.dotfiles/_local/AGENTS.local.md
